From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:11:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: honor the secondary BSS MLD interface address
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a secondary BSS establishes the first link of an MLD,
hostapd_setup_bss() passes its link BSSID to hostapd_if_add() and
copies it into the MLD address. This ignores the configured mld_addr,
unlike hostapd_driver_init() for the first BSS of an interface.

With pWHM, the selected MLD interface can belong to another radio.
The first established guest link then overwrites wlan1.2's intended
MLD address with wlan0.2's link BSSID. On a shared wiphy, bringing up
the dormant wlan0.2 encounters the duplicate netdev address:

  Could not set interface wlan0.2 flags (UP): No error information

Use a nonzero configured MLD address for interface creation or reuse,
while retaining the link BSSID in own_addr for hostapd_drv_link_add().
Initialize the MLD address from the returned interface address. When
bssid is omitted and use_driver_iface_addr is set, the configured MLD
address replaces driver allocation. Allocate the link address separately
by incrementing the inherited address and skipping configured BSSIDs,
using the existing next-available-BSSID policy. Otherwise own_addr would
retain the previous BSS's address when addr becomes non-NULL.

Leave the existing address selection in place when mld_addr is unset,
and keep the existing-MLD borrowing path ahead of the new selection.
Limit the override to !first, where setup adds the first MLD link.
The first == -1 single-BSS ADD path keeps the netdev address equal to
the BSSID. Non-MLD and first-BSS initialization are unchanged.

The nl80211 reuse path already sets the requested hardware address,
including a down/set/up fallback, so it needs no additional MAC update.
Keep the inherited driver-context reset immediately before if_add;
the address selection does not depend on that context.

Fixes: 3d0cc612fcbd ("AP MLD: Support cohosted ML BSS")
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 044b08df9bf9..af9b0fb7fc19 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1527,6 +1527,18 @@ static int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd, int first,
 					   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
 				goto setup_mld;
 			}
+
+			if (!first && !is_zero_ether_addr(conf->mld_addr)) {
+				/* The netdev no longer supplies an automatic link
+				 * address. Allocate it as for other BSSes. */
+				if (!addr) {
+					do {
+						inc_byte_array(hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+					} while (mac_in_conf(hapd->iconf,
+							     hapd->own_addr));
+				}
+				addr = conf->mld_addr;
+			}
 		}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -1554,8 +1566,7 @@ static int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd, int first,
 			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 				   "Setup of first link (%d) BSS of MLD %s",
 				   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
-			os_memcpy(hapd->mld->mld_addr, hapd->own_addr,
-				  ETH_ALEN);
+			os_memcpy(hapd->mld->mld_addr, if_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 		}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	}
